# Audit Trail / Audit Log — mandatory product behaviour

Clari5 AML has an **Audit Trail / Audit Log** module (Administration). Agents authoring Excel, use cases, or Playwright **must** assume **every user/system action** is logged here — without the user re-stating it.

UI references:
- List + filters: `docs/reference/audit-trail-list.png`
- **View Changes** detail modal: `docs/reference/audit-trail-view-changes.png`

## Every action is audited

Any meaningful action across modules — including **login/logout**, **Save / Create / Edit / Delete-Deactivate / Activate**, **maker submit**, **checker Approve/Reject**, navigation-critical admin actions, and other module operations — must produce an Audit Trail row (or rows) with correct module/user/action context.

When a module change has field-level data impact, **View Changes** must show those changes (before/after or current/proposed style content under **DATA STATE CHANGE**). For actions with no field payload (e.g. some login events), the modal may show “No field-level data change recorded…” — still assert the header identity fields.

Do **not** write Expected Results that omit audit logging for mutating or security-relevant actions unless FSD explicitly exempts them.

## List / grid columns (assert when verifying the log)

| Column | Captures |
|--------|----------|
| **Date & Time** | When the action occurred |
| **Module** | Module / sub-module path (filterable; includes **4-Eyes Maker Checker**, KYC, Screening, Administration, etc.) |
| **User ID** | Actor who performed the action |
| **Source IP** | Client / source IP |
| **Action** | Action performed (link/label, e.g. LOGIN, create/edit/approve) |
| **Reference ID** | Technical / business reference for the event |
| **Reason / Remarks** | Justification or system remark (aligns with maker **Business Justification** when that was the reason) |
| **Details** | **View Changes** control → opens detail modal |

Filters available: Search, Module dropdown, Date From/To, Advanced Filters; also Columns / Export as shown in live UI.

## View Changes modal fields

| Field / section | Captures |
|-----------------|----------|
| Title / breadcrumb | Action path context |
| **DATE & TIME** | Event timestamp |
| **MODULE** | Module label |
| **REFERENCE ID** | Reference for the audited object/action |
| **AML USER ID** | System user id |
| **USER NAME** | Display name |
| **SOURCE IP ADDRESS** | Source IP |
| **DATA STATE CHANGE** | Field-level before/after (or current/proposed) change detail when applicable |
| **REASON CODE / REMARKS** | Reason / remarks / justification |

## Relationship to 4-Eyes Maker-Checker

Mutating actions still **pend** in 4-Eyes until Approve (`.cursor/rules/maker-checker-4eyes-mandatory.mdc`). Audit Trail separately records the maker submission, checker decision, and resulting data-state change with the detail fields above. Audit **Reason / Remarks** and **DATA STATE CHANGE** should be consistent with maker justification and Current/Proposed values when those apply.

## Excel / Stage 0

For mutating (and other auditable) happy-paths when coverage includes audit:

1. After the action (and after Approve when the case verifies post-approval state), open **Audit Trail**.
2. Filter/search to the module/user/time/reference as needed.
3. Expected: a matching row with Date & Time, Module, User ID, Source IP, Action, Reference ID, Reason/Remarks.
4. Open **View Changes** and assert modal identity fields + **DATA STATE CHANGE** content for the change (or honest “no field-level change” when that is the live behaviour).

Dedicated Audit Trail module TCs must cover list columns, filters, and View Changes detail — not only “page loads”.

## Playwright / generator / healer

- Prefer shared POM/helpers for Audit Trail list + View Changes; discover locators on the live module.
- When Excel expects audit evidence, assert list row fields and modal sections — do not stub with “audit page visible” alone.
- Do not heal by removing audit asserts or treating missing audit rows as pass.

See also: `.cursor/rules/maker-checker-4eyes-mandatory.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/excel-coverage-mandatory.mdc`.
